{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/348090-ex3-alternative-abyssal-patrons","id":348090,"title":"Ex3: Alternative Abyssal \"Patrons\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-23T00:34:15-08:00","id":348090,"title":"Ex3: Alternative Abyssal \"Patrons\"","content":"If Ex3 gives you the opportunity, who would you like to swear allegiance to <i>besides</i> the canon Deathlords?<br /> <br /> I'm really hoping we get more options for Abyssal character backgrounds in Ex3, certainly I hope to see truly independent deathknights becoming an easier thing to justify, but if you were a free agent and a celestial champion of undeath who would you fight for? No bad answers, non-canon Deathlords welcome.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd want to work for the Eternal Order of Manacle and Coin. Masters of Jade heavily implied this ghostly order of economists is much older than the Guild and perhaps even wealthier in their sphere of influence. Working for them might be like playing a grim reaper/ tax collector who <i>always</i> collects and can never be bargained with. Alternatively a rogue abyssal might make an entire story out of opposing them and their ancient bonds of servitude which preserve but pervert the dead under their sway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T01:23:30-08:00","id":348117,"title":"","content":"Two things:<br /> <br /> Firstly, apparantly independent Abyssals is going to be easier than it was in previous editions.<br /> <br /> Secondly, I don't mind the Abyssals having the Deathlords as their patrons. The problem is, however, that most of the Deathlords are too similar to one another, or not fleshed out enough. Most of them seem interested in 'Destroying Creation' or not doing Anything, and those sorts of types are not very interesting to work for/with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T02:40:13-08:00","id":348145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/348090-ex3-alternative-abyssal-patrons?p=348117#post348117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two things:<br /> <br /> Firstly, apparantly independent Abyssals is going to be easier than it was in previous editions.<br /> <br /> Secondly, I don't mind the Abyssals having the Deathlords as their patrons. The problem is, however, that most of the Deathlords are too similar to one another, or not fleshed out enough. Most of them seem interested in 'Destroying Creation' or not doing Anything, and those sorts of types are not very interesting to work for/with.</div> </div> </div> </div>aye that's why it's a good thing that there exists four unnamed deathlords for St's and players to create their own deathlords to work for.<br /> if i where to work for a non canon deathlord patron i guess the one i would work for would be the craftsman of genocide (one of my custom deathlords) since he actually goes out in person to recruit his abyssals and more or less goes and take the role of the nice old grandpa (for his abyssals at least) and raises those with potential and then turns them into abyssals.<br /> he doesn't really go and mess with his deathknights (except if they do something really stupid then he scolds them unless they keep doing it then he get's nasty).<br /> oh and he is smart enough to work together with the other unnamed deathlords since the way i play it they where buddies in life (except one of them but hey he might be freaky but he is handy to have on your side).<br /> <br /> after the craftsman i would probably work for the madman of the arena (another one of my deathlords) since well you will NEVER incur his wrath (except if you use an archery type weapon against him or near him if you work for him) even if you literally stab him in the face with a grand daiklave since he is kinda obsessed with fighting, so he is proud of you if you messed with one of the other deathlords (except if it happens to be one of his allies or if you lost) he is filled with joy if you made a great enemy (especially if it's right behind you and you tell him in person) and you will not be leaving his arena with bad equipment since he makes sure to armor and arm his servants/&quot;sparring&quot; partners with the best gear he can give them.<br /> <br /> now it's hard to chose witch one of the last two i would like to work for the least but i think my third choice would be the watcher (yup another one of my deathlords).<br /> he sees you, you can not hide from him, you can not run from him, YOU ARE DUST BEFORE HIM... so yeah not great if you want to be independent to serve someone that is basically the eye of sauron combined with the most extreme police stat in history with ridiculous necromantic powers on top.<br /> his deathknights only ever anger him ONCE because after a single punishment they rather die than fail (so yeah basically he is all you dislike in a deathlord kindledRadial).<br /> <br /> and last of the deathlords I've made that i would serve would be the reaper of the mortal harvest since well...<br /> HE IS A COMPLETE AND UTTER PSYCHO MADMAN OF A SCIENTIST.<br /> he managed to fetter his lunar mate's ghost inside a tree made of still living and screaming humans that suffer unbelievable torment every second of their immortal existence(yeah they/it can't die) oh and his lunar suffer all of their torments combined because he likes the taste of the fruit that he harvests from the tree... so yeah he is nasty.<br /> and he experiments on everything especially his deathknights meaning that yeah they have some interesting abilities but well lets just say it's not a pleasant thing.<br /> <br /> otherwise if i where to just serve someone else than a deathlord of any kind it would be Sijan without a doubt since first of you can help being a mediator for the dead second you can help the black watch too keep the piece and third you will probably be as safe as you can be from the deathlords since well there is a lot of powerful dead individuals in Sijan.<br /> like Varan's legion, even if they won't leave Sijan they will be more than happy to beat up anyone who serves the deathlords if they start messing with you (especially if they serve the lion)<br /> <br /> sorry for the wall of text...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T03:25:04-08:00","id":348148,"title":"","content":"Dual Monarchs.<br /> <br /> That is all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I'M SORRY, I CAN'T HEAR YOU OVER THE SOUND OF HOW MANY MALFEAS CHARMS I HAVE!!!</b><i>~King Crazy Genius</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/345-kandagger","name":"Kandagger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T05:40:26-08:00","id":348202,"title":"","content":"The Department of Endings, perhaps.<br /> Maybe one of the more moral of Stygia's council members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T07:44:30-08:00","id":348318,"title":"","content":"The Dual Monarchy has always fascinated me, I'd love to play an underworld centric Abyssal working with (openly or secretly as the ST demands) the Four.<br /> <br /> Then again, my thoughts on Abyssals and theUnderworld have been pretty prolific on the boards..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T07:53:54-08:00","id":348327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/348090-ex3-alternative-abyssal-patrons?p=348117#post348117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly, I don't mind the Abyssals having the Deathlords as their patrons. The problem is, however, that most of the Deathlords are too similar to one another, or not fleshed out enough. Most of them seem interested in 'Destroying Creation' or not doing Anything, and those sorts of types are not very interesting to work for/with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same. I'm find with Deathlords being the default, but independent &quot;ronin&quot; Abyssals being such more supported as a baseline.<br /> <br /> As in, not all independent Abyssals have run from their Deathlord master; some slipped the leash and may be presumed MIA while other Exaltations were never bound to a Monstrance to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T08:03:06-08:00","id":348332,"title":"","content":"He Whose Wings Are Night, a Day Caste retained by the Council of Entities but whose true patron is Nexus itself, wielding the power of death to wage a shadow war against foes like a depraved raksha harlequin, a murderous crocodile-man, and a monocled Guild merchant prince.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":