v> </div> </div> </div>I've been saying rah-KHAN.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T18:25:25-08:00","id":350226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/348090-ex3-alternative-abyssal-patrons?p=350034#post350034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've been saying rah-KHAN.<br /> <br /> And stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>RAKAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAN","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T18:30:15-08:00","id":350247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/348090-ex3-alternative-abyssal-patrons?p=348369#post348369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At no point am I going to advocate anything with regards to the canon Deathlords in this thread because I already talked until I was blue in the face about their problematic Ex2 canon in my last thread. Suffice it to say for the purposes of this topic that I'm assuming that the canonical Deathlords will still be around in Ex3 and they will still have deathknights but that some new setting element will be adopted that will easily justify abyssal &quot;ronin&quot; as Zelbinnean puts it and these characters will safely be able to pledge themselves to entities which are not the Deathlords without fear of immediate termination or suffering eternal.</div> </div> </div> </div>To re-rail this topic, I think I'll set that there are going to be many differences in how Deathlords are presented and conceptualized in Third Edition, and one of the effects of this is that they might be people you <i>want</i> to be the knights of, even if you aren't a sadistic killer or a true believer. For example, I've got a concept kicking around for an Abyssal loyal to the Dowager, but whose deeds in Creation earn them a heroic reputation, and rightly so. Instead of &quot;serve the Deathlords&quot; being one pole of your spectrum of play options, it's an entire spectrum unto itself (plus all the possibilities of being independent).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T20:58:37-08:00","id":350361,"title":"","content":"Thats true the ex3 deathlords may be so different from their ex2 incarnations that simply &quot;serving one's deathlord&quot; may be a varied play style in and of itself. I certainly hope that will be the case. Id love, for example, if the ex3 Silver Prince actually suffered from &quot;buying his own salespitch&quot; as an undead dogooder such that I could play a midnight caste with a major goal of pushing him that extra foot into actual heroism. Sort of a &quot;purehearted squire saving her jaded master&quot; thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T21:24:54-08:00","id":350381,"title":"","content":"I would be fine working for my custom deathlord the forge master of everlasting torment as he is generally uncaring and gives you tons of experimental artifacts. That said I would also love to work for stygia (again also the orphan) or sijan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1166-korekore","name":"korekore","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1166_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T05:23:18-08:00","id":350572,"title":"","content":"My seafaring game disregards the existence of Island Five; the group's Abyssal is a Skullstone orphan, so she's legally a foster child of the Silver Prince. She makes a point of praying to him daily, and though she's not biologically his daughter (as far as she knows), she still refers to him as &quot;Father.&quot; <br /> <br /> Then again, she's also a necrosurgeon who impressed the Silver Prince enough to earn the Black Exaltation by <i>operating on herself</i>. Visuals-wise, imagine a boltless, female Franken Stein from <i>Soul Eater</i>, only her coat is made of behemoth leather with plates of soulsteel.<br /> <br /> I felt a little too constrained by as-written Silver Prince in 2e; hopefully Ex3's version will be able to appear as a caring father to someone without it being a blatant &quot;EXPECT BACKSTAB AHEAD!&quot; warning to their players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-26-2014, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T05:44:12-08:00","id":350594,"title":"","content":"The patron of The Feather in the Storm is whoever currently holds her contract which is sealed with a Moonshadow Oath. This has ranged from major players such as the Guild and the Timeless Order to ordinary people who were simply in the right place at the right time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T19:00:19-08:00","id":351172,"title":"","content":"Another angle I'd like to see played up would be abyssals serving the dead in areas where ancestor worship has been stamped out. There wad the canon moonshadow in the Ex2 core but I'd love to see more of this like an abyssal in Rathis who campaigns for those who didn't fit into the cycle of reincarnation and who have effectively been told that their plight is self-indulgent sin. There are some parallels there with mental illness and addiction in our world, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T00:54:21-08:00","id":351428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/348090-ex3-alternative-abyssal-patrons?p=351172#post351172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another angle I'd like to see played up would be abyssals serving the dead in areas where ancestor worship has been stamped out. There wad the canon moonshadow in the Ex2 core but I'd love to see more of this like an abyssal in Rathis who campaigns for those who didn't fit into the cycle of reincarnation and who have effectively been told that their plight is self-indulgent sin. There are some parallels there with mental illness and addiction in our world, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>aaaaaah yes this concept is nice i actually have a character that is more or less that the &quot;mad mortrician&quot;, he buries the dead on both sides and makes sure people respect their honored dead, or he buries them a bit to early...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T05:12:32-08:00","id":351538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/348090-ex3-alternative-abyssal-patrons?p=351172#post351172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another angle I'd like to see played up would be abyssals serving the dead in areas where ancestor worship has been stamped out. There wad the canon moonshadow in the Ex2 core but I'd love to see more of this like an abyssal in Rathis who campaigns for those who didn't fit into the cycle of reincarnation and who have effectively been told that their plight is self-indulgent sin. There are some parallels there with mental illness and addiction in our world, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell yes! (obligatory ten characters)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron-crowns.obsidianportal.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://exalted-golden-shackles-iron...dianportal.com</a> Visit Golden Shackles, Iron Crowns; a 3rd Edition Exalted Campaign ongoing since 2014","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2711-janissary87","name":"Janissary87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2711_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T09:09:18-08:00","id":353775,"title":"","content":"I have a game that is Dynasty Warriors 8: Exalted! and its successor game So You Wanna Save Tang China. In that game, the Abyssals are empowered by the Sha, which are a sort of spirit group not on the Celestial Bureaucracy; the sort of random Land of Wind and Ghosts that ravage china by being outside of traditional means. They want to destroy China's ruling system and its denizens with equal force, but otherwise are greedy spirits hungry for the joys of life (guess who Dong Zhuo served as a Dusk Caste!). With the game now set in investigating and being diplomats to the Abbasaid Caliphate, the Abyssals that will be featured also include servants of the fallen Sumerian/Babylonian/Akkadian pantheons, as well as Zoroastrian daevas. Say hello to Neverborn versions of Irkalla and Angra Mainyu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/566-the-third-fetich","name":"The Third Fetich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar566_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T12:43:20-08:00","id":354018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Third Fetich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/348090-ex3-alternative-abyssal-patrons?p=353775#post353775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a game that is Dynasty Warriors 8: Exalted! and its successor game So You Wanna Save Tang China. In that game, the Abyssals are empowered by the Sha, which are a sort of spirit group not on the Celestial Bureaucracy; the sort of random Land of Wind and Ghosts that ravage china by being outside of traditional means. They want to destroy China's ruling system and its denizens with equal force, but otherwise are greedy spirits hungry for the joys of life (guess who Dong Zhuo served as a Dusk Caste!). With the game now set in investigating and being diplomats to the Abbasaid Caliphate, the Abyssals that will be featured also include servants of the fallen Sumerian/Babylonian/Akkadian pantheons, as well as Zoroastrian daevas. Say hello to Neverborn versions of Irkalla and Angra Mainyu.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very cool idea! In one of my games we introduced the idea of &quot;banished gods&quot; which are gods who have been stripped of their holdings in Heaven but who persist in Creation by actively cultivating their cults. I had the Norse Aesir filling that role in mine but from what little I know about Babylonian lore that sounds like a good fit too!<br /> <br /> I feel like abyssals serving &quot;fallen gods&quot; has another good angle: underworld gods. We know these exist but are rare; basically these are gods of heaven with enough work ethic to immigrate to the Underworld where their functions are easier, like the canon god of drownings. We don't hear much about these gods, if they have a bureaucracy that they follow, what it looks like, how much more/less effective ghost cults are for them, etc. If we could see more about them in Ex3 I'd love to see a King Enma persona in there that I could serve as a put-upon Moonshadow ala <i>Hozuki no Reitetsu.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T13:41:37-08:00","id":354069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kindledRadial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/348090-ex3-alternative-abyssal-patrons?p=354018#post354018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like abyssals serving &amp;quot;fallen gods&amp;quot; has another good angle: underworld gods. We know these exist but are rare; basically these are gods of heaven with enough work ethic to immigrate to the Underworld where their functions are easier, like the canon god of drownings. We don't hear much about these gods, if they have a bureaucracy that they follow, what it looks like, how much more/less effective ghost cults are for them, etc. If we could see more about them in Ex3 I'd love to see a King Enma persona in there that I could serve as a put-upon Moonshadow ala <i>Hozuki no Reitetsu.</i></div> </div> </div> </div> You know, combine this with the &quot;Five Days Darkness as the Underworld's Unconquered Sun&quot; idea I've heard bandied about, and I think we've got something interesting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T20:09:48-08:00","id":354348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/348090-ex3-alternative-abyssal-patrons?p=354069#post354069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You know, combine this with the &quot;Five Days Darkness as the Underworld's Unconquered Sun&quot; idea I've heard bandied about, and I think we've got something interesting...</div> </div> </div> </div>That is starting to sound like a canonical Underworld good guy faction which is not toothless which I DO like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T21:01:21-08:00","id":354406,"title":"","content":"I would sort of like the idea of playing an abyssal who was functionally roped into serving the role sidereals do for the celestial bureaucracy, but for the underworld equivelent. One who was a savant and astrologer and had open diologue with gods in life, and in death was made to become the arbitrator and moderator for the various underworld tainted gods (if even being a thing, which i think there should be.), celestial gods whose purviews intersect with the underworld (like a god of evicerations, etc), and the other inhabitants of the underworld while still attempting to keep other abyssals and the like from mucking up the underworld equivelent of the celestial fate workings<br /> <br /> Which is to say, serving no entity in specific but serving the grand broken machine that is the underworl'ds ceiling and 'stars'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4499,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4499-willowpanda","user":"Willowpanda","date":".  for completeness 12-30-2014, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4499-willowpanda","name":"Willowpanda","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4499_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T14:40:04-08:00","id":355149,"title":"","content":"I have to say, Willowpanda, that idea intrigues me too. Ever since the Black Treatise mentioning gods abandoning Creation and aspecting themselves towards death, I had wanted to see more of them in the Underworld. I love the idea of an Abyssal working with some of these gods and doing Calendar-related work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}